## Adapted dependencies — MIT (permissive, redistributable)

This section catalogs every project whose work has been
**adapted into the desktop's source tree** (as opposed to
inherited verbatim from `hermes-desktop` or vendored as a
runtime npm dep). Two subsections follow:

1. **Skills ecosystem** — six MIT-licensed upstream projects
   whose `SKILL.md` content has been adapted into the
   desktop's agent-runtime skills layer at
   `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. The 19 skills in this
   group are *prose* adaptations (Cubecloud-original SKILL.md
   bodies derived from the upstream skill descriptions and
   content; no upstream prose is copied verbatim).
2. **Reference-only** — four projects that were *studied*
   during the V2.3 / V2.4 design work but **not** adapted
   into the source tree. Retained from the prior revision of
   this NOTICE for attribution continuity; the skill
   ecosystem above does not promote any of these to a
   "vendored" status.

In addition, the `ar-autoresearch` skill ships a **functioning
Python reference harness** at `ar-autoresearch/harness/`. That
harness is the one place in the desktop repo where adapted
upstream *code* (not just prose) is shipped, and it is
catalogued separately under "Bundled functioning reference
code" below. The harness is reference code the agent may
run on a developer machine; it is not loaded by the desktop,
not linked into the Electron app, and not required for any
desktop feature to work.

