### Bundled functioning reference code (the autoresearch Python harness)

The `ar-autoresearch` skill is the only skill in the 20-skill
ecosystem that ships a *functioning code* reference, not just
prose. The harness lives at
`.agents/skills/ar-autoresearch/harness/` and preserves
Karpathy's upstream `prepare.py`, `train.py`, `pyproject.toml`,
and `README.md` with the data download, BPE tokenizer, GPT
model (rotary embeddings, value embeddings, softcap, ReLU²
MLP), MuonAdamW optimizer, best-fit packing, training loop,
eval, and summary print all intact.

| Path | License | Notes |
|------|---------|-------|
| `ar-autoresearch/harness/prepare.py` | MIT — see `licenses/autoresearch-MIT.txt` | Data download + BPE tokenizer + eval harness. Cubecloud-original modifications: none. SPDX header carries the upstream MIT and a `SPDX-Origin: https://github.com/JZKK720/autoresearch` pointer. |
| `ar-autoresearch/harness/train.py` | MIT — see `licenses/autoresearch-MIT.txt` | GPT model + MuonAdamW + training loop. Cubecloud-original modifications: none. SPDX header carries the upstream MIT and a `SPDX-Origin: https://github.com/JZKK720/autoresearch` pointer. |
| `ar-autoresearch/harness/pyproject.toml` | MIT — see `licenses/autoresearch-MIT.txt` | uv-managed dependency manifest. Cubecloud-original modifications: none. |
| `ar-autoresearch/harness/README.md` | MIT — see `licenses/autoresearch-MIT.txt` | Harness usage notes. Cubecloud-original modifications: documentation comment at the top naming the upstream source and noting the reference-only intent. |

The harness is **not** loaded by the desktop at runtime, **not**
linked into the Electron app, **not** bundled into the
installer, and **not** required for any desktop feature to
work. It exists so the `ar-autoresearch` skill has a working
reference for the agent to experiment with on a developer
machine. Removing the harness would not change the desktop's
build, runtime, or trust surface. The other 19 skills in the
ecosystem are pure-prose adaptations and ship no
corresponding functioning code.

