## Interoperated services (user-installed, network-only, not bundled)

The desktop is a chat client. It does not run a model server
itself. To answer chat requests, the renderer expects the user
to have a local model endpoint already running, or a remote
provider reachable over HTTPS. The desktop does not bundle,
ship, install, or manage any of these — it only speaks their
HTTP protocols. The licenses below govern the user's own
installation, not the desktop's source tree.

| Service | License | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Ollama | MIT | User installs Ollama separately and exposes `http://127.0.0.1:11434`. The desktop only consumes the OpenAI-compatible `/v1/*` and native `/api/tags` endpoints. |
| vLLM | Apache-2.0 | User installs vLLM separately and exposes an OpenAI-compatible server on the loopback. The desktop consumes `/v1/*` only. |
| llama.cpp | MIT | User runs `llama-server` with `--api` separately. The desktop consumes `/v1/*` only. |

The following are listed in some upstream `ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md`
files and have been **removed** from this NOTICE because they
are not part of the desktop's product surface in this revision:

- **Radicale (GPL-3.0)** — no CardDAV/CalDAV integration exists in
  the desktop.
- **OpenSSH** — the desktop does not use SSH to provision
  remote model servers in this revision; remote model servers
  are configured by the user with a base URL.
- **tmux (ISC)** — referenced by upstream "Cookbook" patterns,
  but the desktop has no Cookbook module in this revision.

If a future revision adds any of the above, the rows should be
restored here with a per-feature pointer and a fresh license
text copy under `licenses/`.

